# BrainDump.AI — Cascading Ensemble Flow & Model Training Guide

This guide explains how BrainDump.AI processes text dumps and how the three tiers of Machine Learning models are trained, distilled, pruned, and quantized.

---

## 1. Runtime Inference Flow

When a user submits a raw text dump, the API routes it through a sequential pipeline. If the dump contains multiple distinct thoughts, they are split and processed individually through the cascading ensemble.

```mermaid
graph TD
    Client["User Input (Raw Dump)"] --> API["FastAPI (api/main.py)"]
    API --> Splitter["BlobSplitter (ml/preprocessing/splitter.py)"]
    Splitter --> |"Split by newlines / cues"| Cleaner["TextCleaner (ml/preprocessing/cleaner.py)"]
    Cleaner --> |"Normalized text + verbs + spaCy entities"| Features["FeatureExtractor (ml/preprocessing/feature_extractor.py)"]
    Features --> |"Extracted features"| Arb["Arbitrator (ml/ensemble/arbitrator.py)"]
    
    %% Cascading Logic
    Arb --> T1_Run["Run Tier 1 (TF-IDF + SVM / Keywords)"]
    T1_Run --> T1_Check{"Confidence >= 0.90?"}
    T1_Check -->|Yes| T1_Res["Use Tier 1 Prediction (Speed Path)"]
    T1_Check -->|No| T2_Avail{"Is Tier 2 SLM Available?"}
    
    T2_Avail -->|Yes| T2_Run["Run Tier 2 (Quantized SLM)"]
    T2_Avail -->|No| T3_Avail
    
    T2_Run --> T2_Check{"Confidence >= 0.85?"}
    T2_Check -->|Yes| T2_Res["Use Tier 2 Prediction (Quality Path)"]
    T2_Check -->|No| T3_Avail{"Is Tier 3 BERT Available?"}
    
    T3_Avail -->|Yes| T3_Run["Run Tier 3 (BERT Teacher)"]
    T3_Avail -->|No| Default["Fallback (T1/T2 Max Confidence)"]
    
    T3_Run --> Majority{"Majority Vote (T1, T2, T3)"}
    Majority --> T3_Res["Use Tier 3 Oracle Decision"]
    
    %% Post-Inference
    T1_Res --> Action["ActionEngine (ml/ensemble/action_engine.py)"]
    T2_Res --> Action
    T3_Res --> Action
    Default --> Action
    
    Action --> DB["Persist to SQLite & log metrics"]
    DB --> Response["Return JSON response to Frontend"]
```

### Components in Action:
1. **[api/main.py](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/api/main.py)**: Loads all models into memory once at startup (`lifespan` function).
2. **[BlobSplitter](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/ml/preprocessing/splitter.py)**: Splits blocks of text into individual thoughts.
3. **[TextCleaner](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/ml/preprocessing/cleaner.py)**: Normalizes text, performs part-of-speech tag analysis (for verbs), and extracts entities.
4. **[FeatureExtractor](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/ml/preprocessing/feature_extractor.py)**: Calculates feature scores such as urgency or question flags.
5. **[Arbitrator](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/ml/ensemble/arbitrator.py)**: Routes tasks through the Cascading Tiers based on confidence margins.
6. **[ActionEngine](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/ml/ensemble/action_engine.py)**: A rule-based engine that maps the predicted category, entities, and feature scores to actionable next-step suggestions.

