## 2. Model Training & Compilation Pipeline

The core philosophy of BrainDump.AI is running **entirely local, lightweight models**. To achieve this, it uses a **Knowledge Distillation** and **Model Compression** pipeline.

```mermaid
graph TD
    Dataset["Labeled Training Data"] --> T1_Train["Train SVM (training/train_tier1.py)"]
    T1_Train --> T1_Model["models/tier1_svm.pkl (TF-IDF + SVM)"]
    
    Dataset --> T3_Train["Train BERT Teacher (ml/slm/01_teacher/train_teacher.py)"]
    T3_Train --> T3_Model["models/teacher_bert/ (Full BERT Model)"]
    
    %% Distillation Flow
    T3_Model --> |"Generates soft targets"| T2_Distill["Distill Student (ml/slm/02_distillation/distill_train.py)"]
    T2_Distill --> T2_Student["models/student_distilled/ (MiniTransformer)"]
    
    %% Pruning Flow
    T2_Student --> T2_Prune["Prune Weights (ml/slm/03_pruning/run_pruning.py)"]
    T2_Prune --> T2_Pruned["models/student_pruned/ (Sparse Student)"]
    
    %% Quantization Flow
    T2_Pruned --> T2_Quant["Quantize Model (ml/slm/04_quantization/quantize_dynamic.py)"]
    T2_Quant --> T2_Quantized["models/student_quantized.pt (Quantized SLM, ~8ms latency)"]
```

### Explaining the Training Phases

#### Phase A: Tier 1 (Fast & Simple) — [ml/ensemble/tier1_tfidf.py](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/ml/ensemble/tier1_tfidf.py)
* **How it works (Day 1)**: If no model is trained, it does regex overlap checks with hardcoded keywords (`KEYWORD_RULES`). The confidence is capped at `0.75` to indicate to the Arbitrator that this is a rule-based prediction.
* **How it trains**: Running `python training/train_tier1.py` fits a TF-IDF vectorizer + an SVM (Support Vector Machine) on the dataset. It saves the resulting scikit-learn pipeline as a `.pkl` file. When loaded, it outputs actual probability scores for predictions.

#### Phase B: Tier 3 (The BERT Teacher Oracle) — [ml/ensemble/tier3_bert.py](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/ml/ensemble/tier3_bert.py)
* **Role**: Serves as the high-accuracy "ground truth" oracle. It is slow (~280ms) and heavy, but captures complex language structures.
* **Training**: Finetunes a pre-trained BERT transformer on the training dataset.

#### Phase C: Tier 2 (The Distilled & Quantized Student SLM) — [ml/ensemble/tier2_slm.py](file:///c:/Users/majed/OneDrive/Documents/ML%20Projects/braindump.ai-main/ml/ensemble/tier2_slm.py)
* **Role**: Runs extremely fast (~8ms) on a single CPU core, while retaining ~95% of the BERT Teacher's accuracy.
* **How the Student is created**:
  1. **Knowledge Distillation**: A smaller student model (MiniTransformer) is trained to mimic both the hard labels of the dataset and the "soft probabilities" output by the heavy BERT Teacher model. This transfers the teacher's soft decision boundaries to the student.
  2. **Weight Pruning**: Unimportant weights (near-zero values) in the neural network are pruned (zeroed out) to create a sparse network structure.
  3. **Dynamic Quantization**: Converts model weight representations from 32-bit floating point numbers (`FP32`) to 8-bit integers (`INT8`). This shrinks the model size by ~4x and speeds up CPU matrix math dramatically.
